]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3152052c-7362-5223-aca9-8a01e7e7f9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3152052c-7362-5223-aca9-8a01e7e7f9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284666} :answer-field/id #uuid "442afccf-24e4-5d09-93e5-c718143dd5e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284665} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a28605-c9b8-5efa-afa6-187fc985a2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28605-c9b8-5efa-afa6-187fc985a2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284668} :answer-field/id #uuid "35b77f1d-87f0-5c45-b6d3-5c7dae154f18" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3286c20-7601-5ef5-bdef-b24bd472d849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3286c20-7601-5ef5-bdef-b24bd472d849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284670} :answer-field/id #uuid "e11516c6-d9ec-50fa-87c6-93648d7a0975" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c2dcecf-d016-574a-86d8-44ea5655e5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c2dcecf-d016-574a-86d8-44ea5655e5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284672} :answer-field/id #uuid "300bcb4e-f3f8-5dbb-a6ad-e8a3a620fc02" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5806b8d3-8c2c-520f-9045-92a3abcd749c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317632" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+4=7 \\\\ -2x+6z-1=8 \\\\ 7y-5z+2=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $9$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $7$ | $-5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+0z=3 \\\\ -2x+0y+6z=9 \\\\ 0x+7y-5z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031eef6d-4a20-5f86-9d93-fbacd2a5e7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=0,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284675} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ecbad9-d272-546a-8dd9-c59736456a30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=0,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284676} {:answer/id #uuid "ae5c8a96-5bfe-5193-8464-cc3e4bf87209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284677} {:answer/id #uuid "ef458ff9-26f0-5ab6-add2-40b9f3417d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=1,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284678} {:answer/id #uuid "979cf3b8-ed5c-537f-af19-1cec515dd31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ecbad9-d272-546a-8dd9-c59736456a30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=0,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284676} :answer-field/id #uuid "15def9e3-2c68-561d-982f-2811fcc193bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3e71ee9-4e24-52af-a780-70c10d095991" :question/math-academy-id "q-75500" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2y+3z=7 \\\\ x+z=-1 \\\\ 3z-2x+y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & b & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-2y+3z=7 \\\\ x+0y+z=-1 \\\\ -2x+y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=0,\\,c=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5893f99-81c5-5686-b70f-8cb0d331ab51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284682} {:answer/id #uuid "8fbe0f41-adb7-54d0-b9da-6d7c04d5f815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284683} {:answer/id #uuid "c9749fbc-d72d-5dcf-9730-3f1137de0196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284684} {:answer/id #uuid "e96c0798-49ad-5fd7-8178-dab1cb6411f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284685} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff95514-3350-5e00-b4c5-13916f8593c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fbe0f41-adb7-54d0-b9da-6d7c04d5f815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284683} :answer-field/id #uuid "15706fde-5495-5dbb-acd9-125e60ea3309" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d56da79a-73d5-5555-8061-ba75678fe9af" :question/math-academy-id "q-75506" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-y+z=1 \\\\ 2z+y+x=-1 \\\\ 3y-z+x=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y+z=1 \\\\ x+y+2z=-1 \\\\ x+3y-z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba9a8ba9-1bd5-5f68-b6cb-1f1e4215e723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-3,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284689} {:answer/id #uuid "39c2f160-bc4c-5776-861a-df33fafc6eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284690} {:answer/id #uuid "22e3dbe9-e5da-5528-ab60-5b64e7d8875b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=-3,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284691} {:answer/id #uuid "b342889e-bd35-5879-9627-85e1a25c1969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-5,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284692} {:answer/id #uuid "21ee5e2f-0993-5436-bfc9-a5d1d239ecc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39c2f160-bc4c-5776-861a-df33fafc6eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284690} :answer-field/id #uuid "64089744-0c3c-5609-9604-1ed6c4e789e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffe699fb-01ac-54c3-88e2-a1b2fa943327" :question/math-academy-id "q-75509" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y-5x+3z=-1 \\\\ x-3y=3 \\\\ -3y+2z-x=-5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & a & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & b \\\\ c & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ x-3y+0z=3 \\\\ -x-3y+2z=-5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecb7ab6f-06dd-553d-9b4f-2bf3a5f15be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284696} {:answer/id #uuid "e811c971-b42b-57a3-8cfe-8df18a1e62a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=6,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284697} {:answer/id #uuid "e37462f9-8aaf-5338-a83e-a9cc52290547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284698} {:answer/id #uuid "934cae89-2696-517d-97d2-078985cb6ae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284699} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd35db9-be56-57d7-945a-f5925f7091e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd35db9-be56-57d7-945a-f5925f7091e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284700} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5dbf484-058f-54ae-823c-b19172829282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c19a6cb8-f905-5407-af86-886e3c517cbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-9720" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z=2 \\\\ x+3z-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+y+2z=1 \\\\ 3x+6y-2z=2 \\\\ x-y+3z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3.$"}]}
